<title>HUNGARY: IBUSZ Jan-Sept profits fall in 1996.</title>
<headline>IBUSZ Jan-Sept profits fall in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine-month period ending September 30.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>					Jan-Sept 96	    Jan-Sept 95</p>
<p>    Group operating profit	17.0	   vs	181.1</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit	 112.2	   vs	185.2</p>
<p>    Group tax-payment		0	     vs	 19.7</p>
<p>    Group after-tax profit     112.2	   vs	165.4</p>
<p>    Group net profit	     112.2	   vs	165.4</p>
<p>    Group sales		  3,720	     vs    5,583.4</p>
<p>Group material expenditures</p>
<p>				     2,279.7	   vs    4,181.1</p>
<p>Group personal expenditures</p>
<p>					 593.1	   vs	547.6</p>
<p>    Group depreciation	    76.2	   vs	 78.8</p>
<p>    Group other costs	    707.8	   vs	926.9</p>
<p>    Group other expenditures   124.7	   vs	136.6</p>
<p>    Group financial result	73.9 profit  vs	 31.1 loss</p>
<p>    Group extraordinary profit  21.3	   vs	 25.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Full company name is IBUSZ Idegenforgalmi, Beszerzesi, Utazasi es Szallitasi Rt. Foreign investors held 41.9 percent of IBUSZ on September 30, the remaining shares were owned by Hungarians. The largest Hungarian shareholder was IBUSZ Aktiv Rt, with 19.1 percent, followed by Idegenforgalom 2000 Portfolio Rt, which has a stake of 14.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
